# Memory Workflow

Use organizational memory as long-term memory, not scratch space.

Required flow:

- Recall at session start and before major design decisions or unfamiliar code.
- Give feedback on every recalled memory.
- Recall again after repeated failures with the exact symptom or error.
- Remember durable decisions, facts, patterns, mistakes, and achievements.
- Include namespace, context, relevant files, and source task when writing memory.

If memory tools are unavailable, report that explicitly and continue with local
evidence. Do not pretend memory was read or saved.
